{
  "FormatVersion": 3,
  "Id": "91bb0f8b-593c-557c-9da6-15005722b733"/*VolumeToPointsExample*/,
  "Description": "One torus volume, three outputs side by side. Left: [VolumeToMesh] extracts triangles. Middle: [VolumeToPoints] turns the voxels near the surface into points, drawn together with the boxes of the volume's sparse tree from [DrawVdbBounds] - only where there is surface is there data. Right: [VolumeToTexture3D] bakes a dense 3D texture and [VolumeField] makes it a field that [RaymarchField] draws.\n\nAKA: volume to points, point cloud, voxels, sparse tree, raymarch, 3d texture, convert\n\nTips\n- Smaller VoxelSize means sharper surfaces and more memory and time; start coarse and refine.\n- Level sets store signed distance in world units (negative inside); fog volumes store density.\n- Meshes suit shading and physics, points suit particles, the texture suits raymarching and SDF combinations.",
